# The composed layers that owe no sum, and for which quantity. One row per (composed layer,
# ground), carrying which ground it was and which quantity it lifts.
#
# Read `quantity` before you use this
#   NULL means every quantity is suspended (nobody searched at all, a conversion nobody sized, or a
#   part that is not here); a value means exactly that quantity is (the overlap was found and could
#   not be sized against it, a layer the sum reads leaves it unstated, or a derived part cannot be
#   computed). A caller computing one quantity's sum wants
#   `quantity IS NULL OR quantity = '<that one>'`. ⚠️ Claim "no sum at all"
#   here while the second arm pins `demand` and drops the column, and the claim is true of one arm
#   and false of the other with nothing downstream able to tell.
#
# Why it exists: De Morgan
#   The condition it names otherwise reaches its call sites as a conjunction of two negations, in
#   two different SQL idioms: an `IS DISTINCT FROM` beside a `NOT EXISTS`. That is the most
#   drift-prone shape there is, two ways to say NOT, neither of which names what is being
#   excluded. `NOT a AND NOT b` is `NOT (a OR b)`, so the thing to name is the disjunction: the
#   fusions that are suspended. The callers then anti-join one relation, and adding a ground
#   for suspension is a new file rather than a new clause in two predicates.
#
# Two kinds of ground, one set
#   composition/filed_grounds.sqlc holds the grounds read off what a fusion and its parts file;
#   composition/underived_parts.sqlc holds the one that needs a computation, a part filed
#   `derived` whose figure cannot be derived. Every sum reads both, through this relation. Only
#   composition/suspended_remainders.sqlc reads the first alone, and its header says why.
#
# Run this alone before reading any composition check
#   Every row here is a fusion whose arithmetic is not owed, and a checker reporting a pass on one
#   of these rows is reporting about nothing.
#
# A bag, not a set
#   This is a bag and not a set, which is the whole reason it is two files. One fusion can be
#   suspended on more than one ground (`every-unsized-conversion/shift-capacity` files both an
#   unsearched elimination and an unsized conversion) and it is suspended once. The key here is
#   (composition, composed_layer, quantity, suspended_because); the key a caller almost always
#   wants is the first three, and `composition/suspended_fusions.sqlc` is that projection.
#
# The difference is invisible to almost every caller
#   That is why it needs saying. `EXISTS`, `NOT EXISTS` and `EXCEPT` are blind to multiplicity: a
#   duplicate row changes nothing they compute. A `LEFT JOIN` is not, and a law that counts
#   fusions is not. So the projection is what a counter or a joiner reads, and this file is what a
#   reader who needs the reason reads. A relation nobody has joined on is a multiplicity nobody
#   has checked.
-- the grounds that lift the sum rule: those read off the filing, and a derived part that cannot be computed.
:union(ALL composition/filed_grounds.sqlc, composition/underived_parts.sqlc)
